{
  "slug": "meren-recursion",
  "as_of_decklist_sha256": "c9e7d41682c64e3c2192a3542a2acae94987d70b7d473f3dac429eadc27d0e0c",
  "reading": "NO CHANGE. Swaps cannot get this deck to a turn-6 fatty through Meren, because the gap is deaths. To return a 5-drop at the turn-6 end step, Meren must be out by turn 4 (median cast turn 4, 92.5% cast by turn 6). She then needs about five deaths over her first three end steps, or about three with Winding Constrictor adding one per counter event, and a 5+ creature card must be in the yard. The goldfish averages 1.343 sacrifices by turn 6 and 2.433 experience. The outlet-plus-fodder pair is drawn by turn 6 in 46.6% of games (57.9% with tutors), so the goal reads 14.2% and 1.7%. The two seen fodder and proliferate adds I screened move those rows by +0.4 to +0.9 points and +0.0 to +0.2 points, which is below the clear-upgrade bar. Backing into it: the turn-6 goal is a mulligan and sequencing target (keep outlet plus fodder, tutor for Ophiomancer or Constrictor before a fatty). Turn 7-8 is where the list reaches it today (experience 4.266 at turn 7, 6.628 at turn 8).",
  "log_entries_read": [],
  "axes_engaged": [
    {
      "axis": "creatures",
      "verdict": "adequate",
      "measured": {"value": 41},
      "reading": "41 bodies is plenty of potential fodder. The goldfish only sacrifices tokens, though, so experience grows with the token makers (Bitterblossom, Jadar, Ophiomancer, Scute Swarm, Woe Strider's Goat, Pawn of Ulamog's Spawn) and not with the creature count."
    },
    {
      "axis": "consistency",
      "verdict": "strength",
      "measured": {"value": 0.91},
      "reading": "The turn-3 land drop hits 0.91 and Meren's median cast turn is 4, so the mana is on time. The turn-6 miss happens after she lands, not before."
    },
    {
      "axis": "tutors",
      "verdict": "adequate",
      "measured": {"value": 8},
      "reading": "Eight tutors raise the engine pair's turn-6 rate from 0.466 to 0.579 when used for it, which is the largest lever the goldfish shows here. That makes it a play pattern: Demonic Tutor and Fiend Artisan go to Ophiomancer or Winding Constrictor before a fatty.",
      "citations": [{"rule": "strategy:mulligans.engine-hands", "quote": "100-card singleton means you mulligan to enabler\n*classes*, not named cards; build the redundancy your keeps depend on."}]
    }
  ],
  "cut_candidates": [],
  "add_candidates": [],
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Why is 'a 5+ drop via Meren by T6' (1.7%) so far below 'experience 5+ by T6' (14.2%)? Is it the yard (no 5+ creature card left once Reanimate or Animate Dead has used it), the timing (experience reaching 5 only after the turn-6 end-step trigger), or how the model picks Meren's target?",
      "settled_by": "goldfish",
      "why_it_matters": "If the cause is timing, the turn-5 or turn-6 goal is out of reach for this list, and the honest target is turn 7. If it is the yard, the lever is keeping a binned fatty for Meren rather than spending it on a reanimation spell. That is a play choice, not a swap."
    },
    {
      "question": "The brief says the outlet-plus-fodder pair is drawn by T6 in 67% of games. goldfish_metrics.json's 'THE EXPERIENCE ENGINE drawn' target reads by_turn_6_rate 0.466 (assisted 0.579). Which figure does the 67% come from?",
      "settled_by": "goldfish",
      "why_it_matters": "At 47-58% the drawing gap is still real, and 'the gap is deaths, not drawing' is only half true. Both factors cap the goal row."
    },
    {
      "question": "Chatterfang, Squirrel General (add a 1/1 Squirrel on every token creation) is PARTIAL to the model, so try withheld its rows. On paper it adds roughly one death per token, which is the variable that binds. Is it worth teaching the model, or judging by play?",
      "settled_by": "research-strategy",
      "why_it_matters": "It is the one candidate I found that multiplies deaths per turn at three mana. No figure exists for it, and I have not checked whether it opens a two-card line with this 99."
    }
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "Screened in try (10,000 paired games, cut Zulaport Cutthroat, a drain payoff that is not an outlet, fodder engine, removal or draw): Tendershoot Dryad (seen) experience 5+ by T6 14.2% -> 15.1%, +0.9 pts [+0.7, +1.1]; a 5+ drop via Meren by T6 1.7% -> 1.9%, +0.2 pts [+0.1, +0.2]; worse on killed by T10 (-0.7 pts [-0.9, -0.4]) and a 6+ drop out by T6 (-0.3 pts [-0.4, -0.1]). Evolution Sage (seen) 14.2% -> 14.6%, +0.4 pts [+0.3, +0.6]; via Meren 1.7% -> 1.7%, +0.0 [-0.0, +0.1]. Both are resolvable but small, and neither is a clear upgrade under the pilot's rule. The third screen (Chatterfang) was withheld as PARTIAL, so it has no reading.",
    "No games are logged (deck-notes list is empty), so nothing at the table confirms or contradicts the goldfish's death rate. The goldfish has no opponents' removal, which helps Meren, and no chump attacks, which a real pilot uses for deaths.",
    "The goldfish sacrifices only tokens. A pilot who sacrifices nontoken bodies that Meren will return gets more experience than the model reads, so 14.2% is a floor for skilled sequencing. How much higher is unmeasured."
  ]
}
